### Why these options work well for your family

| Feature | Benefit |
|---------|----------|
| **Room layout** – All listings provide either a suite or an entire apartment with **2 separate sleeping areas** (or a sofa‑bed) so the children have their own space. |
| **Central or well‑connected locations** – Navona, Pantheon, Monti, and Castel Sant’Angelo are within a 10‑minute walk or a single metro stop to the main sights (Colosseum, Vatican, Spanish Steps). Villa Pamphili offers a quieter setting with a park and easy shuttle to Termini. |
| **Family‑friendly amenities** – Kitchens or kitchenettes (A Window on Pantheon, Castel Sant’Angelo, Colosseo Room) let you prepare simple meals; breakfast buffets (Nikis Collection Navona, Villa Pamphili) give a hassle‑free start to the day. |
| **High guest ratings** – All properties score **≥ 8.7/10**, indicating consistent quality and good service. |
| **Price range** – From **≈ US $270/night** (Colosseo Room) up to **≈ US $614/night** (A Window on Pantheon). This gives you flexibility whether you prefer a budget‑friendly stay or a more luxurious apartment. |

### Next steps

1. **Pick your preferred property** – If you want a central boutique hotel with a suite, **Nikis Collection Navona** is a solid mid‑range choice. For a fully self‑catered experience, **A Window on Pantheon** or **Castel Sant’Angelo Apartments** are ideal.  
2. **Reserve early** – These rooms are limited, especially the family‑sized suites/apartments, so I recommend booking as soon as possible.  
3. **Add extras** – Most of these hotels can arrange:  
